---
import Shell from '../layouts/Shell.astro';
import Brand from '../components/Brand.astro';
---
<Shell title="Brand studio · vector refinement 03"><div class="wrap">
<div class="page-head"><p class="eyebrow">Brand studio · vector refinement 03</p><h1>One identity.<br/><em class="highlight">Room for each language.</em></h1><p class="lead">Sea-blue words. Laterite emphasis. English and Odia with space to stand on their own.</p></div>
<p class="notice">Updated to your direction: separate English and Odia marks, Nila Sagara main headings and buttons, Mankada Pathara highlights. The book-and-boat symbol is now drawn as a clean vector, with outlined English and Odia lettering; final visual approval remains open.</p>
<section class="section" style="padding-top:15px"><p class="eyebrow">01 · Two separate signatures</p><div class="brand-grid">
<div><div class="lockup"><Brand/></div><p class="option-note"><strong>English · Utkal Project</strong>The default signature for the English website. A sea-blue wordmark, with the laterite book-and-sail symbol.</p></div>
<div><div class="lockup"><Brand language="or"/></div><p class="option-note"><strong>Odia · ଉତ୍କଳ</strong>A standalone Odia signature in Noto Serif Odia. The established Odia word is used here; a translated full project name has not been invented.</p></div></div>
<div class="screen-proof"><div><p class="eyebrow">24 px symbol proof</p><img class="small-mark" src="/assets/brand-v3/symbol-small.svg" alt="Book and boat small-size proof"/></div><div class="proof-dark"><Brand tone="reverse"/></div><p style="font-size:12px;max-width:300px">The reverse preview uses a single light colour. A simplified small-size vector omits fine page detail. The reversed signature is a separate light-colour SVG.</p></div></section>
<section class="section" style="padding-top:0"><p class="eyebrow">02 · Colour in use</p><h2>Grounded in the sea.<br/><em class="highlight">Warmed by the earth.</em></h2><div class="palette"><div class="swatch" style="background:var(--sea)"><span lang="or">ନୀଳ ସାଗର</span><div>Nila Sagara<br/><small>#1D4658 · Main headings, wordmarks and primary buttons</small></div></div><div class="swatch" style="background:var(--earth)"><span lang="or">ମାଙ୍କଡ଼ା ପଥର</span><div>Mankada Pathara<br/><small>#91462F · Emphasis, sail symbol and warm accents</small></div></div><div class="swatch" style="background:var(--olive)"><span lang="or">ଶୁଖା ଘଷି</span><div>Sukha Ghasi<br/><small>Olive #74633B · Straw #C1A263</small></div></div></div><div class="actions"><a class="button" href="/">See the updated homepage ↗</a></div><p style="margin-top:20px;font-size:13px">The supplied “World is One” image guides the balance of colour and white space. Existing working hex values are retained, rather than claiming an exact pixel match.</p></section>
<section class="section" style="padding-top:0"><p class="eyebrow">03 · Building an Odisha feeling</p><h2>Something to wear.<br/><em class="highlight">Something to remember.</em></h2><p class="lead">An Odia word on a favourite tee. The sea on a morning cup. A flower whose story leads back to a place.</p><div class="brand-decisions"><h3>The next refinement</h3><p>Review the proportions of these two separate signatures. Sea & Stone brings the emblem, wave rhythm and separate scripts to four product designs. Botanical motifs remain a later, researched collection.</p></div></section>
<section class="prose section" style="padding-top:0"><h2>The story keeps growing.</h2><p><a href="/assets/brand-v3/utkal-project-en-colour.svg" download>English vector signature</a> · <a href="/assets/brand-v3/utkal-project-or-colour.svg" download>Odia vector signature</a> · <a href="/assets/brand-v3/symbol-small.svg" download>Small symbol</a></p><p>The palette began with your stone, sea, straw and cooking-fuel associations. This iteration changes how those same colours work together: Nila Sagara carries the reading and actions, while Mankada Pathara supplies the warmth and emphasis.</p><p>Direction: Ahimanikya Satapathy. Design assistance: AI. Earlier bilingual experiments and the original palette story remain in the project KB.</p></section>
</div></Shell>
